{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans","id":1375491,"title":"Calling Technocracy Fans.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-18T14:49:36-07:00","id":1375491,"title":"Calling Technocracy Fans.","content":"Are you excited for Technocracy Reloaded? What you want to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T16:35:10-07:00","id":1375512,"title":"","content":"Having backed M20 and being disappointed with it's contents I have no plan to back the technocracy book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T17:09:14-07:00","id":1375516,"title":"","content":"While I have some issues with M20, I generally approve of what it's done. I'm looking forward to Technocracy Reloaded as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T18:22:40-07:00","id":1375523,"title":"","content":"Overall, I've enjoyed roughly 80% of all the content that constitutes M20 (i.e., core book, HDYDT, Book of Secrets, Gods &amp; Monsters, Book of the Fallen.) The parts I haven't liked mostly have to do with system/mechanics changes that I think &quot;nerfed&quot; Mages in favor trying to make them scale in power somewhat with other supernaturals (Mages are rare, naturally squishy, and sphere magic is dangerous and expensive--let them trounce vampires a little); or to attempt to 'bake in' to the system certain constraints on magic intended to make the game jibe with the <i>de rigueur</i> social politics of today, by making it more difficult or impossible for players engage in &quot;problematic&quot; conduct. Mind you, these social politics are my social politics, but the implementation feels patronizing, and out of step with the larger tonal aspects of the WoD.<br /> <br /> Having said that (since other commenters mentioned either liking or not liking M20 thus far) -- I'm really looking forward to any and all additional 20th Anniversary content for any of the lines, but <i>mostly </i>M20, and what this Technocracy book to delve into Threat Null, overhaul the treatment of social media, fake news, etc., as it integrates into the system and Technocratic paradigm; I want to know more about how the Technocracy is entrenched into human governments and the intelligence community; I want to know what's going on with John Courage. And (if I'm being REALLY honest), I want stat blocks. I want HIT Marks and combat cyborgs of all stripes; war clones; cybertooth tigers; I want mech suits, and Rob Liefeld-style huge, honkin' energy weapons; I want an expansion of the Build-A-Ship system in <i>Void Engineers (Rev.)</i>; I want systems for space combat.<br /> <br /> I'm probably asking for too much--but my enjoyment of the books will basically be proportional to the degree to which one or more of the foregoing appear in its pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T19:36:44-07:00","id":1375532,"title":"","content":"I have doubts that we'll be seeing any more of Threat Null: my suspicion is that Technocracy Reloaded will be following the metaplot ideas that Brucato had with his New Millennium notion: the Avatar Storm happened, but it's long since died down (which is the main reason I don't expect to see Threat Null); the Traditions have set up a new Council headquartered in New Zealand, and many of them have renamed themselves; and most importantly where the Technocracy is concerned, a (probably Technephandi-inspired) purge of \u201cinsufficiently loyal\u201d Technocrats is or has recently taken place in the guise of a reorganization of the Union (resulting in a new take on the Conventions), leading to the Knights of Avalon formally jumping ship as the new Navalon Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T20:47:00-07:00","id":1375540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375523#post1375523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want stat blocks. I want HIT Marks and combat cyborgs of all stripes; war clones; cybertooth tigers; I want mech suits, and Rob Liefeld-style huge, honkin' energy weapons; I want an expansion of the Build-A-Ship system in <i>Void Engineers (Rev.)</i>; I want systems for space combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I want to have the rules to build my own versions of all of that, or to run a game with only HIT Marks, if that's something I decide to do. And I want stats for all the models of them. And space combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T06:30:10-07:00","id":1375593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375532#post1375532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have doubts that we'll be seeing any more of Threat Null: my suspicion is that Technocracy Reloaded will be following the metaplot ideas that Brucato had with his New Millennium notion: the Avatar Storm happened, but it's long since died down (which is the main reason I don't expect to see Threat Null); the Traditions have set up a new Council headquartered in New Zealand, and many of them have renamed themselves; and most importantly where the Technocracy is concerned, a (probably Technephandi-inspired) purge of \u201cinsufficiently loyal\u201d Technocrats is or has recently taken place in the guise of a reorganization of the Union (resulting in a new take on the Conventions), leading to the Knights of Avalon formally jumping ship as the new Navalon Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be cool, though <i>hardly</i> metaplot agnostic. I mean, that would be a major set of developments to the metaplot. If they continue with the &quot;toolbox&quot; approach, I would expect them discuss Threat Null is some way or other. Having said that, I really like the idea of the Knights of Avalon/Navalon thing. Where is that stuff? Like, where can I read about Brucato's vision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T08:13:27-07:00","id":1375615,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the book dug deep into the philosophy behind the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T08:44:44-07:00","id":1375619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitromidas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375540#post1375540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! I want to have the rules to build my own versions of all of that, or to run a game with only HIT Marks, if that's something I decide to do. And I want stats for all the models of them. And space combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More of this, please. HIT Marks, Space combat, ships, exploration, Men in Black, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T09:15:33-07:00","id":1375624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375593#post1375593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would be cool, though <i>hardly</i> metaplot agnostic. I mean, that would be a major set of developments to the metaplot. If they continue with the &quot;toolbox&quot; approach, I would expect them discuss Threat Null is some way or other. Having said that, I really like the idea of the Knights of Avalon/Navalon thing. Where is that stuff? Like, where can I read about Brucato's vision?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all in M20, if you know where to look. The New Horizon Council is described on pages 145\u2013147; Brucato revealed in various posts (mostly on the M20 Facebook page) that his head-canon tends to go along the lines of the \u201ccompromise position\u201d for <i>the Dimensional Anomaly and a \u201cKinder, Gentler Technocracy\u201d</i> (p.169) \u2014 that is, \u201cThe Storm has faded, but the scars remain\u201d. Of note, that Future Fate ends on the note that \u201cthe Union <i>has</i> become more humane and is looking at long-term reform. If the Nephandi are in charge, however, that might not be a good thing at all\u2026\u201d. <br /> <br /> Under \u201cTechnocratic Dissidents\u201d, the Harbingers of Avalon are described as being \u201ca half-step away from leaving the Technocracy and reforming under a new name: Navalon.\u201d <br /> <br /> In <i>A Technocratic Upgrade?</i> (p.185), \u201cIt's a good bet that the pending re-org comes courtesy of the Nephandic Inner Circle. What better way could there be, after all, to rattle loose the stubborn idealists than to reorganize the entire organization and find out who and where those malcontents might be? such shake-ups always have casualties, and if a bit of red ink winds up spilling over groups like Project Invictus, the Friends of Courage, and the Harbingers of Avalon, well, that's just the cost of doing business.\u201d<br /> <br /> And one of the <i>Potential Recruits</i> section of the Disparates (pp.199\u2013200) is \u201c<i>Navalon</i>, a breakaway group of idealistic Technocrats who revere the example of King Arthur and despise the corruption of their previous Union.\u201d<br /> <br /> As for this not being \u201ctoolboxy\u201d, times have changed over the last five years; and I suspect that Technocracy Reloaded is going to take a less metaplot-agnostic approach than we've seen so far \u2014 though I suspect that lip service will still be paid to \u201cif you don't want to do it this way, you don't have to\u201d, so perhaps Threat Null won't be ignored entirely. But I'll be surprised if they get more than a brief mention here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T10:39:55-07:00","id":1375646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375615#post1375615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the book dug deep into the philosophy behind the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T11:13:09-07:00","id":1375652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375615#post1375615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the book dug deep into the philosophy behind the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt we'll see this \u2014 in the form of the Technocratic Focus, and its section on Paradigms and Practices. <i>Technology Holds All the Answers</i> will be ubiquitous; it is, after all, the heart and soul of the Technocracy's philosophy. But I expect to see variations on other Paradigms and some new ones that have a Technocratic spin to them. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping (but not expecting) that they address what I consider to be the single biggest flaw in the way the Technocracy has been handled in the past: namely, that they've been presented as being fundamentally and objectively <i>wrong</i>, with the lower ranks being ignorant of the True Nature of Reality and the higher ranks lying about it. I've gone into depth about how I think it ought to be addressed elsewhere, so I won't belabor the point here; but I <i>do</i> want it addressed better than it has been in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T11:57:38-07:00","id":1375662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375523#post1375523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And (if I'm being REALLY honest), I want stat blocks. I want HIT Marks and combat cyborgs of all stripes; war clones; cybertooth tigers; I want mech suits, and Rob Liefeld-style huge, honkin' energy weapons; I want an expansion of the Build-A-Ship system in <i>Void Engineers (Rev.)</i>; I want systems for space combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping we'll get clearer treatments of the various Technocratic Practices; in particular, the Syndicate's Art of Desire and Hyper-economics is one area that lots of people tend not to get. <br /> <br /> I'm expecting to see Wonders and Constructs from Iteration X and the Progenitors (or whatever they're going to be called after the re-org); I'm hoping to see some examination on the distinction between \u201cProcedure and Instrument\u201d on the one hand and \u201cGadget, Invention, or Device\u201d on the other. As well, the Iteration X Constructs should cover the hypertech potential of AI, giving us robotics as well as cyborgs. The Revised Progenitors book already covers most of what I'd like to see for the bio-tech Wonders and Constructs. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see more about Extraordinary Citizens, M20-style. I'd like, but <i>really</i> don't expect, to see advanced education techniques from the NWO or its successor that allow Enlightened Scientists and Extraordinary Citizens alike to learn and perform individual Procedures, blurring but not erasing the distinction between them. And I'd really like an examination of the Technocracy's system for shifting Reality Zones and getting their innovations incorporated into the Consensus. <br /> <br /> And yes, something on hypertech vehicles (including, but not limited to, Void Ships and Walkers) employed by the Void Engineers would be great, including expansions on vehicular combat and chases. Along with rules for alien environments and aliens \u2014 though that might be a bridge too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T05:43:14-07:00","id":1375794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I'm 1000% down with everything you said, and frankly, didn't realize how much I wanted certain things until I read them in your comment--and despite my desire for basically <i>kewl stuff!</i>, I overwhelmingly would also like this addressed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375662#post1375662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the distinction between \u201cProcedure and Instrument\u201d on the one hand and \u201cGadget, Invention, or Device\u201d on the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we've played Techocrats at my table, we sort of avoided the issue of discussing what the Technocrats think is happening when they use a technological device to perform magic--I mean, when they pull out a gun and &quot;Hot Shot&quot;, do they think there's something built into the gun that permits them to do that? Does the person who built the gun (assuming it's a special, albeit non-magical/non-enlightened Technocrat gun like an X5 or something) think they built some part of it to perform the effect? It always seems like technomancers (from Sons of Ether to Technocrats) are always just painting a cardboard washing machine box with gunmetal gray spray paint, then drawing on some knobs, and making some random wires stick out of it, and they're like <i>voila!</i><i> A transmogrifier! </i>It just seems hard to wrap my head around how the hell they think what they're doing is different from the traditions, other than from an aesthetics/milieu/trappings standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T12:37:39-07:00","id":1375843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375794#post1375794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we've played Techocrats at my table, we sort of avoided the issue of discussing what the Technocrats think is happening when they use a technological device to perform magic--I mean, when they pull out a gun and &amp;quot;Hot Shot&amp;quot;, do they think there's something built into the gun that permits them to do that? Does the person who built the gun (assuming it's a special, albeit non-magical/non-enlightened Technocrat gun like an X5 or something) think they built some part of it to perform the effect? It always seems like technomancers (from Sons of Ether to Technocrats) are always just painting a cardboard washing machine box with gunmetal gray spray paint, then drawing on some knobs, and making some random wires stick out of it, and they're like <i>voila!</i><i> A transmogrifier! </i>It just seems hard to wrap my head around how the hell they think what they're doing is different from the traditions, other than from an aesthetics/milieu/trappings standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been explained before.... But by and large the difference is a technomancer has a theory behind their inventions. This theory can be utterly ridiculous, for example you could claim that when painted blue, a sheet of steel emits bluons. These Bluons are a form of radiation, that when they strike molecules at the right frequency can change elements into other elements. However they can be contained and controlled by sheets of steel painted red.<br /> <br /> Patently ridiculous. But you do have a theory. Now for the Etherites they revel in just how out there their theories can be and still be 'true.'<br /> <br /> Technocrats approach on the other hand is different. They want to 'define all.' their grand quest is to come up with one universal framework that explains everything so by and large their hypertech isn't so much subverting reality as it is intended to take advantage of rules that weren't out of beta yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:06:11-07:00","id":1375956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1375652#post1375652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping (but not expecting) that they address what I consider to be the single biggest flaw in the way the Technocracy has been handled in the past: namely, that they've been presented as being fundamentally and objectively <i>wrong</i>, with the lower ranks being ignorant of the True Nature of Reality and the higher ranks lying about it. I've gone into depth about how I think it ought to be addressed elsewhere, so I won't belabor the point here; but I <i>do</i> want it addressed better than it has been in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a secret no many are aware about Mage: the Ascension : it is a game about spirituality. The original traditions are based not just on real-world cultural area, but on the spirtituality of these cultures. The word &quot;Arete&quot;, even if commonly translatted into &quot;virtues&quot;, mean, in hermetica, as the betterment of one self, the connection to the divine inside, the elevation of the soul to its principle. In that optic, the Technocracy is objectivly wrong, as are the Nephandis and the Marauder, btw. As for technomagick, as the many real-world spirtuality have for principle the detachment of the material world, well, draw your own conclusion.<br /> <br /> But it is were the game and the setting really shine : you can be objectivly wrong, and still act, do things and having influence on the world all around you. And in our Age of Solipsism, this is a powerful thing to said.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T08:07:13-07:00","id":1375968,"title":"","content":"And that was fine in the first edition, when the Technocratic Union was the monolithic Man oppressing the heroic underdog mages. It hasn't been that for a long time; certainly not in M20, where the Technocrats are presented on even footing with the Traditions and the Disparates as protagonists (as opposed to the Nephandi and the Marauders, both of whom are still presented as antagonists).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:38:19-07:00","id":1376003,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I'm concerned. I love the Technocracy and I thought the Revised Convention Books were the best material we've seen to date regarding the Technocracy. But Phil wrote on a Facebook post a few months back that he didn't want to write it as them being &quot;The REAL good guys&quot; and that no matter how well meaning they will ultimately still be fascists. I'm hoping we at least see some good Iteration X material given they are my favorites and their Convention Book pales in comparison. I want to be excited but we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T14:39:03-07:00","id":1376009,"title":"","content":"Is it coming out soon? Technocracy Reloaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T15:05:11-07:00","id":1376014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376003#post1376003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm concerned. I love the Technocracy and I thought the Revised Convention Books were the best material we've seen to date regarding the Technocracy. But Phil wrote on a Facebook post a few months back that he didn't want to write it as them being &amp;quot;The REAL good guys&amp;quot; and that no matter how well meaning they will ultimately still be fascists. I'm hoping we at least see some good Iteration X material given they are my favorites and their Convention Book pales in comparison. I want to be excited but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is that there aren't any \u201creal good guys\u201d; <i>everyone</i>, including the Traditions, is flawed. <br /> <br /> My earlier post was about wanting the Technocracy to have a metaphysical leg to stand on, <i>not</i> whether or not they have the moral high ground. Even in the\u201cKinder and Gentler\u201d Revised Conventions, you still had the NWO engaged in institutional brainwashing and the Syndicate more interested in profit than ethics; all they did was to take the worst edge off of the more problematic groups (e.g., no more Computer running Iteration X, no more SPD, and no more mass infiltration of the Void Engineers by Deep Umbral sympathizers). <br /> <br /> But in terms of less reprehensible Technocrats, that's where I expect Navalon to come in: they'll still be flawed, and not the non-existent hypothetical \u201ctrue heroes\u201d of the game; but they won't be fascistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T16:19:35-07:00","id":1376022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376014#post1376014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that there aren't any \u201creal good guys\u201d; <i>everyone</i>, including the Traditions, is flawed.<br /> <br /> My earlier post was about wanting the Technocracy to have a metaphysical leg to stand on, <i>not</i> whether or not they have the moral high ground. Even in the\u201cKinder and Gentler\u201d Revised Conventions, you still had the NWO engaged in institutional brainwashing and the Syndicate more interested in profit than ethics; all they did was to take the worst edge off of the more problematic groups (e.g., no more Computer running Iteration X, no more SPD, and no more mass infiltration of the Void Engineers by Deep Umbral sympathizers).<br /> <br /> But in terms of less reprehensible Technocrats, that's where I expect Navalon to come in: they'll still be flawed, and not the non-existent hypothetical \u201ctrue heroes\u201d of the game; but they won't be fascistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, That's actually what I'm hoping for. But the comment of &quot;They're not the REAL good guys&quot; took me as a detraction from that. Too often we get the Traditions being &quot;the good guys&quot; and that's all I'm saying I want to move away from. Saying the Technocracy are fascists is, to me, saying they are the bad guys. If we get a more grey area where no one is the good or bad guys then I'm actually happier with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T17:26:36-07:00","id":1376036,"title":"","content":"Oh, there are definitely bad guys in the M20 setting; if nothing else, you have the Nephandi. And I won't be at all surprised if <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> ends up returning the Union to a more purely fascistic model \u2014 but you'll also have Navalon as a home for your Enlightened Scientists who are more like the Revised Conventions than the Technephandi-dominated Union: that is, the same sorts of Paradigms and Practices, but without the \u201cwe can and will run your life better than you\u201d mission statement that the Union is about to go all in on. <br /> <br /> If I'm right, the Navalon Scientists won't technically be Technocrats anymore, as that's literally \u201cgovernment by the technical elite\u201d and Navalon will at the very least be unable, and probably unwilling as well, to do anything resembling governing for the foreseeable future. <br /> <br /> But though they'll reject the Technocracy's aims, they'll still be Technocrats in the sense of their understanding and practice of Enlightened Science; and that will set them apart from the Society of Ether and the Mercurial Elite, both of which long ago embraced the Traditions' unifying Paradigm that \u201cWe are all Gods in Disguise\u201d (also known as the Purple Paradigm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T17:29:32-07:00","id":1376038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376009#post1376009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it coming out soon? Technocracy Reloaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's coming out Soon\u2122: it's nearly through Onyx Path's development process, and the plan currently is to Kickstart it \u2014 though plans aren't final until they've been executed. Exactly when it will be Kickstarted is still unknown as far as I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T19:31:51-07:00","id":1376055,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T07:35:11-07:00","id":1376108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376036#post1376036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, there are definitely bad guys in the M20 setting; if nothing else, you have the Nephandi. And I won't be at all surprised if <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> ends up returning the Union to a more purely fascistic model \u2014 but you'll also have Navalon as a home for your Enlightened Scientists who are more like the Revised Conventions than the Technephandi-dominated Union: that is, the same sorts of Paradigms and Practices, but without the \u201cwe can and will run your life better than you\u201d mission statement that the Union is about to go all in on.<br /> <br /> If I'm right, the Navalon Scientists won't technically be Technocrats anymore, as that's literally \u201cgovernment by the technical elite\u201d and Navalon will at the very least be unable, and probably unwilling as well, to do anything resembling governing for the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> But though they'll reject the Technocracy's aims, they'll still be Technocrats in the sense of their understanding and practice of Enlightened Science; and that will set them apart from the Society of Ether and the Mercurial Elite, both of which long ago embraced the Traditions' unifying Paradigm that \u201cWe are all Gods in Disguise\u201d (also known as the Purple Paradigm).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn't a huge fan of Navalon when it was first introduced in the Guide to the Technocracy. In real life my background is Physics and I work in the Semiconductor Industry and I'm tired of anything science and technology related having to have a mystic bent just to be deemed good. I think Phil is great when he writes mystic oriented groups but, honestly, I don't have much faith in him to represent scientific and technological groups well given his past work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T09:27:38-07:00","id":1376120,"title":"","content":"My point is that I think that the extent of the \u201cmystic bent\u201d that Navalon will have is that they'll be aligned loosely with several mystical societies (the Disparates) in order to fight the Technocracy's depredations. The whole point of the Disparates in my view is that they <i>don't</i> subscribe to the Traditions' Grand Unified Theory of Magick, and each faction is completely free to pursue its own philosophy and practices as they always have, without compromise. All they ask is that they give each other shelter and aid when the bad guys show up and start messing with them. <br /> <br /> If I'm right, a Navalon technician will be indistinguishable in terms of Focus from an Iteration X technician. The difference will be the fact that the former will be fighting Hit Marks while the latter will be deploying them. There won't be anything mystical in the way Navalon's Scientists do what they do any more than there's anything mystical in the way the Technocracy's Scientists do what <i>they</i> do, because their theories and practices will be identical; the only difference will be what goals they pursue. <br /> <br /> Which is why <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> would be a good place to talk about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T07:40:48-07:00","id":1376261,"title":"","content":"I don't think the bad version of the Technocracy are fascists, but the worst forms of capitalism.<br /> <br /> I mean, now of all times &quot;fascism&quot; should be recognised to mean a specific thing, and the Technocracy have to be as far away as one can get from some of the basic tenets like, say, the idealisation of a made up pre-lapserian past.<br /> <br /> Unless there's something I misunderstood about them, there's no time in the past where Y was &quot;great&quot; that they want to make it again in their eyes; greatness lies entirely in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T09:08:07-07:00","id":1376269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376261#post1376261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the bad version of the Technocracy are fascists, but the worst forms of capitalism.<br /> <br /> I mean, now of all times &quot;fascism&quot; should be recognised to mean a specific thing, and the Technocracy have to be as far away as one can get from some of the basic tenets like, say, the idealisation of a made up pre-lapserian past.<br /> <br /> Unless there's something I misunderstood about them, there's no time in the past where Y was &quot;great&quot; that they want to make it again in their eyes; greatness lies entirely in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 100% this for me. I think too many people conveniently ignore how much social progress has taken place under the Technocracy, but as you note there's also the concers of the worst forms of Capitalism. I think the dark Cyberpunk future is a good expression of how bad things could get under the Technocracy but it shouldn't be conveyed as Fascist.<br /> <br /> It's one of the things I appreciated from the Revised Convention books was acknowledging the faults while showing how they try to do good at the same time. The Feminist progress within the NWO is a great example to me as it shows more women moving into higher positions but you still have the issues of a patriarchy built in. Add onto that how the NWO and Progenitors try to move towards Universal Healthcare but they have to contend with the Syndicate that want a paid insurance model instead and you see how the internal politics are part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Much more realistic and interesting imho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T11:33:50-07:00","id":1376280,"title":"","content":"Each Convention has its own dystopian future; and the bad side of the Technocracy as a whole depends on which one of them dominates. <br /> <br /> \u201cThe worst forms of capitalism\u201d? That's what you get when the dark side of the Syndicate emerges. But when the dark side of the NWO emerges, you get a totalitarian surveillance state. The dark side of the Void Engineers is the evils of empire: a military state that enslaves and exploits its subjects to further empower the elite. It's possible to integrate these three into a single dystopian future; but it's also possible for one or two to represent a dark future without the others. <br /> <br /> And if the dark sides of Iteration X and/or the Progenitors are truly let loose, you won't have to worry about politics or economics: the former will literally turn us all into components in a machine (see \u201cThe Matrix\u201d, but substitute \u201cprocessing node\u201d for \u201cbattery\u201d) assuming the machines don't wipe out organic life entirely (hello, Skynet!), and the latter will see the emergence of a literal Gaia hive-mind as the entire bio-mass of the planet gets incorporated into a single life form that is to us as we are to our cells (Isaac Asimov's <i>Foundation's Edge</i>). I kind of do want to see <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> address Threat Null, as the Autopolitans and Transhumanity highlight what can happen if their respective Conventions go overboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T13:11:49-07:00","id":1376296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376261#post1376261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the bad version of the Technocracy are fascists, but the worst forms of capitalism.<br /> <br /> I mean, now of all times &quot;fascism&quot; should be recognised to mean a specific thing, and the Technocracy have to be as far away as one can get from some of the basic tenets like, say, the idealisation of a made up pre-lapserian past.<br /> <br /> Unless there's something I misunderstood about them, there's no time in the past where Y was &quot;great&quot; that they want to make it again in their eyes; greatness lies entirely in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree completely. The Technocracy tried that on for size in WWII and it went horribly bad. I'm fairly certain the experiences from that time inoculated the Union against that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T14:01:43-07:00","id":1376307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitromidas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376296#post1376296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree completely. The Technocracy tried that on for size in WWII and it went horribly bad. I'm fairly certain the experiences from that time inoculated the Union against that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The New World Order is still very much pushing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T21:09:17-07:00","id":1376365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376280#post1376280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Convention has its own dystopian future; and the bad side of the Technocracy as a whole depends on which one of them dominates. <br /> <br /> \u201cThe worst forms of capitalism\u201d? That's what you get when the dark side of the Syndicate emerges. But when the dark side of the NWO emerges, you get a totalitarian surveillance state. The dark side of the Void Engineers is the evils of empire: a military state that enslaves and exploits its subjects to further empower the elite. It's possible to integrate these three into a single dystopian future; but it's also possible for one or two to represent a dark future without the others. <br /> <br /> And if the dark sides of Iteration X and/or the Progenitors are truly let loose, you won't have to worry about politics or economics: the former will literally turn us all into components in a machine (see \u201cThe Matrix\u201d, but substitute \u201cprocessing node\u201d for \u201cbattery\u201d) assuming the machines don't wipe out organic life entirely (hello, Skynet!), and the latter will see the emergence of a literal Gaia hive-mind as the entire bio-mass of the planet gets incorporated into a single life form that is to us as we are to our cells (Isaac Asimov's <i>Foundation's Edge</i>). I kind of do want to see <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> address Threat Null, as the Autopolitans and Transhumanity highlight what can happen if their respective Conventions go overboard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of that is still pretty much capitalism, which is more than just finance.<br /> <br /> I would need to be sold on the idea that Iteration X is compelled by a deeper ideology before I dismissed it as ultimately an exercise in harnessing capital to enshrine and endlessly expand the power of its elite with only the shallow veneer of an ethos; silicon valley Gordon Gecko trying to provide the terminology by which a bunch of people that are already on board can rationalize that their greed is an affirmative, transformative thing rather than benefitting their relentless and unexamined need for growth.<br /> <br /> Not really a rhetoric intended to appeal to the masses, because their input is irrelevant anyway, but still the kind that a large chunk of them will uncritically adopt to justify the status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T21:21:10-07:00","id":1376368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376307#post1376307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The New World Order is still very much pushing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so the New World Order wants to create a worldwide surveillance state. To what purpose? What would it be that they would be surveilling people for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T23:31:24-07:00","id":1376375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376365#post1376365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of that is still pretty much capitalism, which is more than just finance.<br /> <br /> I would need to be sold on the idea that Iteration X is compelled by a deeper ideology before I dismissed it as ultimately an exercise in harnessing capital to enshrine and endlessly expand the power of its elite with only the shallow veneer of an ethos; silicon valley Gordon Gecko trying to provide the terminology by which a bunch of people that are already on board can rationalize that their greed is an affirmative, transformative thing rather than benefitting their relentless and unexamined need for growth.<br /> <br /> Not really a rhetoric intended to appeal to the masses, because their input is irrelevant anyway, but still the kind that a large chunk of them will uncritically adopt to justify the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really don't see a difference between \u201cusing capital to empower the elites\u201d and \u201cturning people into machine parts\u201d? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376368#post1376368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so the New World Order wants to create a worldwide surveillance state. To what purpose? What would it be that they would be surveilling people for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that what's currently under discussion is the worst aspects of each Convention: it's more than just surveillance; it's propaganda, too. And control of the education system. All toward the goal of making the Masses easier to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T09:19:42-07:00","id":1376404,"title":"","content":"Iteration X wants to help people evolve through technology and are basically Transhumanists. The &quot;turning people into machine parts&quot; is really more of a Tradition propaganda stance. Which, let's be honest, the worst descriptions of the Technocracy are USUALLY (not always) Tradition propaganda because they're usually set up as the protagonists and the Technocracy as the antagonists. Even the Revised book portrayed them as antagonists despite books like Vampire Revised including the other Clans in their book as potential PCs.<br /> <br /> Can the Technocracy be the antagonists, of course, but that doesn't mean they really are as bad as they have been sold to be. Conversely, the Traditions aren't as good as they have been sold to be. I mean, let's look at this a bit more objectively (insofar as anything like this can be) and note that the Traditions are literally trying to bring us backwards to an older time. Thus, the Traditions by definition are not intrinsically pro-progress which includes things like social progress. On the other hand, actions have been taken in society in the name of progress that have not worked well for everyone usually because they can't predict every possible outcome.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think the real holdback for all the groups is, ironically, the very Sleepers Mages are trying to save. But Sleepers are also the ones that get hurt by the actions of Mages which is how Mages are monsters just like Vampires and Werewolves. Our way is the right way is pretty universal with all Mages. So for me it's just tedious anytime the Technocracy gets demonized because after 4 editions it just feels like &quot;yeah, we get it, you don't like them. Ooga booga science and technology bad&quot;. And don't get me started on the nonsense that all Science is only done by Etherites. That's an insult to the Scientific Community if I ever heard one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T09:40:59-07:00","id":1376408,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I should have put the \u201cBearing in mind that what's currently under discussion is the worst aspects of each Convention\u201d clause at the <i>top</i> of my post. And yes, <i>at its worst</i>, Iteration X <i>is</i> turning people into machine parts. The Tradition propaganda has a kernel of truth in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T13:41:34-07:00","id":1376430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376404#post1376404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for me it's just tedious anytime the Technocracy gets demonized because after 4 editions it just feels like &quot;yeah, we get it, you don't like them. Ooga booga science and technology bad&quot;. And don't get me started on the nonsense that all Science is only done by Etherites. That's an insult to the Scientific Community if I ever heard one.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts on this: <br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union isn't just representatives of science and technology; it also has an agenda.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Technocracy:</i> the government or control of society or industry by an elite of technical experts.</div>If you aren't in favor of an elite of technical experts running society or industry, you're not a Technocrat. This is true even if you favor science and technology. The problem is that Mage doesn't currently include a faction that represents science and technology but <i>doesn't</i> have the Technocratic agenda. So thus far, players who want their characters to be Scientists but not Technocrats have had to be rebels within the Union, Etherites, VAs, or (as of M20) Orphans with a scientific Focus. There are reasons why each of the latter three options are unacceptable to many, which up to now has left players who want Enlightened Scientists who aren't Technocrats with only one option: dissidents within the Union. <br /> <br /> That's where Navalon comes in, hopefully: if it turns out the way I'm hoping it will, Navalon will be advocates of science and technology without the technocratic agenda, and also without the fringe sciences that the Society of Ether embraces or the mystical elevation of information that defines the VAs. <br /> <br /> Would I have chosen the name \u201cNavalon\u201d for them? No. Nor would I have put the mythology of Avalon as a defining inspiration for the faction. Their Focus will almost certainly incorporate \u201cBring Back the Golden Age\u201d (M20 pp.568\u2013569), which I can understand people having a problem with. That said, I personally don't have too much of a problem with it \u2014 though my inclination for the \u201cGolden Age\u201d that they want to bring back would be the Order of Reason rather than Avalon. The notion of \u201cbringing back\u201d the <i>ideals</i> that Avalon (or the Order of Reason) represents strikes me as a reasonable rallying point for former Technocrats who have fled the Union. <br /> <br /> So while I don't think it's <i>exactly</i> what I'm looking for, I do think that it's close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-26-2020, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:40:31-07:00","id":1376512,"title":"","content":"So I am curious are they going to integrate the 5 Metal Dragons, or barely mention them, or even not mention them at all?<br /> <br /> I would personally like more on Technocracy history and evolution. Stuff about how Agents who live like 80 years would see major paradigm and technology shifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want info on how the Technocracy spread throughout the globe from the Renaissance, with things like the 5 Metal Dragons and the rest of the World integrating into the Technocracy..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:44:42-07:00","id":1376514,"title":"","content":"Also info on 100+ year old Technocrats active probably only in the Spirit World.<br /> <br /> And how Technocracy intermingles with things like how Academia spawning the social justice movement, and the changes of words to fit new meanings, and the attempt to update the modern paradigm from Universities to Pop Culture and from there to the whole world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T07:49:17-07:00","id":1376552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376512#post1376512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am curious are they going to integrate the 5 Metal Dragons, or barely mention them, or even not mention them at all?<br /> <br /> I would personally like more on Technocracy history and evolution. Stuff about how Agents who live like 80 years would see major paradigm and technology shifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want info on how the Technocracy spread throughout the globe from the Renaissance, with things like the 5 Metal Dragons and the rest of the World integrating into the Technocracy..</div> </div> </div> </div>From early commentary by Brucato, the Elemental Dragons will indeed be in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>. (To clarify, the Five Metal Dragons is the term used used by the Asian Technocracy to refer to the Western Conventions.) There will also be an African Technocracy. We don't yet know how these pieces fit together, especially with the possibility of a Technocratic reorganization; but there's going to be more to the Technocracy and its history than the European-centric Conventions featured in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T08:18:25-07:00","id":1376556,"title":"","content":"Oh nice thanks for the info. It feels like several conspiracies from around the world would have joined the Order of Reason rather then just concentrating on European Order of Reason spreading everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T08:33:15-07:00","id":1376559,"title":"","content":"I think that's what Brucato is going for, yes: technocracy developed independently in several parts of the world at different times in history, and the story of the Order of Reason is merely how it got started <i>in Europe</i>. The Elemental Dragons have their own history, as does the African Technocracy. As for the present, who knows? It might be that one of the goals of the anticipated reorganization of the Union is to integrate the European, Asian, and African Technocracies into a single, unified whole. I personally hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:44:47-07:00","id":1376587,"title":"","content":"I didn't know about the African Technocracy. That should be really cool especially with the rise of Afrofuturism in Science Fiction literature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T11:01:31-07:00","id":1376590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376404#post1376404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iteration X wants to help people evolve through technology and are basically Transhumanists. The &amp;quot;turning people into machine parts&amp;quot; is really more of a Tradition propaganda stance. Which, let's be honest, the worst descriptions of the Technocracy are USUALLY (not always) Tradition propaganda because they're usually set up as the protagonists and the Technocracy as the antagonists. Even the Revised book portrayed them as antagonists despite books like Vampire Revised including the other Clans in their book as potential PCs.<br /> <br /> Can the Technocracy be the antagonists, of course, but that doesn't mean they really are as bad as they have been sold to be. Conversely, the Traditions aren't as good as they have been sold to be. I mean, let's look at this a bit more objectively (insofar as anything like this can be) and note that the Traditions are literally trying to bring us backwards to an older time. Thus, the Traditions by definition are not intrinsically pro-progress which includes things like social progress. On the other hand, actions have been taken in society in the name of progress that have not worked well for everyone usually because they can't predict every possible outcome.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think the real holdback for all the groups is, ironically, the very Sleepers Mages are trying to save. But Sleepers are also the ones that get hurt by the actions of Mages which is how Mages are monsters just like Vampires and Werewolves. Our way is the right way is pretty universal with all Mages. So for me it's just tedious anytime the Technocracy gets demonized because after 4 editions it just feels like &amp;quot;yeah, we get it, you don't like them. Ooga booga science and technology bad&amp;quot;. And don't get me started on the nonsense that all Science is only done by Etherites. That's an insult to the Scientific Community if I ever heard one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not something Iteration X has ever been about. Iteration X isn't, and never had been concerned with the masses, which was one of those few things that set them apart from the rest of the Technocracy. Even in their old school 'worst' portrayal, they were isolationist rather than expansionist. Because expansion would require they tolerate some level of imperfection.<br /> <br /> Old school evil Iterators are brutal perfectionists with no toleration for weakness or mistakes of any kind. Their entire ethos was different from the rest of the Technocracy in so far as they didn't care about the rest of the world beyond their enclaves, save in maintaining their ties to the rest of the Union.<br /> <br /> In revised, this transformed into becoming more or less the superhero ethos, of having to be strong to be the guardians of humanity. In so far as ever being concerned with humanity, that's how they're related to it. If you step up as a soldier to guard the people, yes they're going to want you to be a perfect metal soldier without weakness's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T11:39:24-07:00","id":1376597,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's the nice ones. The worst of the bunch <i>do</i> want to impose their ideal of perfection on everyone, to the point that what can't be perfected needs to be eliminated. <br /> <br /> But that's the worst of the bunch, the ones who serve as the antagonists that your protagonists need to stop. The more run of the mill ItXer is indeed more of an isolationist in practice: \u201cbefore we can perfect the world, we must first perfect ourselves\u201d. <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't say that this makes them unique. For instance, the Void Engineers also aren't particularly interested in Terran society; they're more concerned with taming the remaining frontiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T14:46:58-07:00","id":1376616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1376552#post1376552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There will also be an African Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wakanda forever.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, it's more Lee and Kirby-style than the recent stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T15:12:59-07:00","id":1376620,"title":"","content":"Very likely. For one thing, the plans for an African Technocracy predate the MCU's Wakanda. Mind you, I don't know what those plans <i>are</i>; only that the very first mention of <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, way back at the end of the M20 Kickstarter, indicated that an African Technocracy would be included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T00:35:45-07:00","id":1383919,"title":"","content":"It seems that tuesday beggins the kickstarter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/insert-punny-title-here-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/insert-punny-title-here-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> Insert Punny Title Here. [Monday Meeting Notes] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/insert-punny-title-here-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/insert-punny-title-here-monday-meeting-notes/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T01:57:21-07:00","id":1383924,"title":"","content":"I have work again so I'll be able to back it! Yay! M20 has been awesome so far and I'm looking forward to TR and as many stretch goals as we can hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T08:47:38-07:00","id":1383960,"title":"","content":"I deliver groceries to people who can't get to the store themselves, so this recent crisis has actually given me <i>more</i> income than usual. I'll definitely be backing Technocracy Reloaded. And hopefully the rest of the country will be getting back on its feet soon enough that it won't just be me and few fortunate others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T10:10:35-07:00","id":1383974,"title":"","content":"Mage: The Podcast has a discussion with Danielle Lauzon and Travis Legge, two contributors to Technocracy Reloaded.<br /> <br /> Might be worth listening to, as the Mage: The Podcast folks talk out what's in the book and what ideas were being explored when writing the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/04/25/technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-preview-with-danielle-lauzon-and-travis-legge/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://magethepodcast.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cropped-test.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/04/25/technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-preview-with-danielle-lauzon-and-travis-legge/\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Mage: The Podcast </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/04/25/technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-preview-with-danielle-lauzon-and-travis-legge/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/04/25/technocracy-reloaded-kickstarter-preview-with-danielle-lauzon-and-travis-legge/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:40:28-07:00","id":1385221,"title":"","content":"In the Road to Hell trilogy of novels I remember having read something about Pentex infiltration in the Syndicate. And also in Guide of Technocracy and the first books of second edition. What happened with that plot? It faded away or it is still a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T03:02:57-07:00","id":1385226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1385221#post1385221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Road to Hell trilogy of novels I remember having read something about Pentex infiltration in the Syndicate. And also in Guide of Technocracy and the first books of second edition. What happened with that plot? It faded away or it is still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Special Projects Division. Has.....disappeared. Like literally and the rest of the Syndicate is freaked by it. But I think Travis said something about their cheques were still going through.........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T08:42:50-07:00","id":1385245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375491-calling-technocracy-fans?p=1385226#post1385226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Special Projects Division. Has.....disappeared. Like literally and the rest of the Syndicate is freaked by it. But I think Travis said something about their cheques were still going through.........</div> </div> </div> </div>There are supposed to be several future fates for the Special Projects Division. The M20 line is intended to pick up those dangling plot threads and see where they'd go in the present day while giving you more than one option. So, if you like Special Projects Division as being the same, just being gone, or something in between, there will be some options in Technocracy Reloaded.<br /> <br /> Travis saying the SPD had disappeared but their checks (U.S. spelling) are still going through was just one of the options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:31:36-07:00","id":1385255,"title":"","content":"And there's also an option where SPD never existed in the first place. <br /> <br /> They're covering all their bases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:46:16-07:00","id":1385258,"title":"","content":"I have read the Sindicate book just a few hours ago, it is very interesting the way the disappearance is depicted, with even their enemies (Invictus) still fighting Pentex without knowing they are gone. Even the Sindicate created a new bureau with the only commitment to cover this fade to black. It is a source of inspiration even more interesting than the original wyrm infestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:50:30-07:00","id":1385259,"title":"","content":"That said, I use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009152-spd-a-new-take\">a radically different version of SPD</a> in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}